# Settings for one PAC Keeper app on Opalstack. Copy this file to
# ~/apps/APPNAME/env and fill it in. The start script reads it.

# The program: the Linux build, from the GitHub release.
PAC_KEEPER="$HOME/bin/pac-keeper"

# The port that the Opalstack dashboard shows for this app. The server
# listens on this computer only; Opalstack's web server passes it the requests.
PAC_BIND="127.0.0.1:PORT"

# The records. Keep them outside ~/apps, and include them in your backups.
PAC_DATA_DIR="$HOME/pac-keeper-data/APPNAME"

# For the public demo (demo.packeeper.ca), turn this on:
#PAC_DEMO=1

# For the hosted server (app.packeeper.ca), turn these on:
#PAC_HOSTED=1
#PAC_BASE_URL="https://app.packeeper.ca"
# Encrypts the hosted server's records. Make it with `pac-keeper new-data-key`,
# and keep a copy in your password manager: without it, nobody can read the
# records or the backups. See "Encrypted records" in the README.
#PAC_DATA_KEY="..."
# The SMTP user is the Opalstack mailbox name, not the email address.
# Write any special character in the password as %XX (for example, @ is %40).
#PAC_SMTP_URL="smtps://MAILBOX:PASSWORD@smtp.us.opalstack.com:465"
#PAC_MAIL_FROM="PAC Keeper <hello@packeeper.ca>"
# Visit counts for the operator (/operator/stats), from the sites' logs:
#PAC_STATS_SITE_LOG="$HOME/logs/sites/packeeper/access.log"
#PAC_STATS_DEMO_LOG="$HOME/logs/sites/pk_demo/access.log"
#PAC_STATS_APP_LOG="$HOME/logs/sites/pk_app/access.log"
#PAC_STATS_GITHUB="sjhewitt/packeeper"

# Hot lunch ordering on the hosted server (a preview, off by default):
#PAC_HOT_LUNCH=1
# Card payments through Stripe Connect. See "Hot lunch" in the README.
#PAC_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY="sk_live_..."
#PAC_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRETS="whsec_account...,whsec_connect..."
#PAC_STRIPE_CLIENT_ID="ca_..."
# Stripe pays each PAC once a week. The weekday of the payout (default monday):
#PAC_STRIPE_PAYOUT_DAY=monday
# Your surcharge on payments through your Stripe, in basis points (100 = 1%) and cents:
#PAC_SURCHARGE_BP=0
#PAC_SURCHARGE_CENTS=0
# PACs can also connect their own Helcim accounts; the server needs nothing for
# that. If you are a Helcim integration partner, for Helcim's revenue share:
#PAC_HELCIM_PARTNER_TOKEN="..."
